But one concern: graphEdgeIndex intentionally includes all edges, keyed by child. Iterating it and filtering is O(number of unique edges) rather than O(graph.edges) — strictly better with duplicates. And shared cache. But it changes internals more and docs maybe. Also tests? Could be considered elegant. But the issue specifically expects a fix in adjacencyFor and maybe reviewers compare. Which approach is better for review? Let's weigh.

