```
interface DiscoveryFrame { readonly node; next: number }
```
and push `{node: edge.parent, next:0}`.

Emission ordering unchanged because DFS order same.

Undo logic: when popping origin frame, pathEdges last is edge into origin. Remove origin from visited. Good. When root reaches origin? candidate===origin precheck in discoverPaths, so collectPaths never called with equal. But collectPaths is private; guard remains. If root==origin, pathEdges empty, pop and stack empty, no undo. Fine.

When frame exhausted (node != origin), pop and undo incoming edge. Root exhaustion no undo. Good.

Cycle detection: visited contains candidate and all nodes on pathEdges, invariant.

Immutability: `frozenPath` copies pathEdges, then continues; okay. `pathEdges.pop()` doesn't affect emitted copy.

